# Web App Lives in `ainexus-web/` — NEVER `web/src`

The React/Vite web app is a **sibling** of this Flutter workspace.

- ✅ CANONICAL (always edit here): `D:\Projects\Android-App\ainexus-web\`
  - This is the deployed repo (`src/`, `package.json`, `Dockerfile`, `vite.config.ts`, `nginx.conf.template`).
- ❌ NEVER edit any `web/src` directory. A legacy "split-brain" copy at
  `ai_nexus/web/src/` caused fixes to silently not ship. It has been removed —
  do not recreate it, and do not edit files under any `web/src` path.
- ℹ️ `ai_nexus/web/` is ONLY Flutter's web shell (`index.html`, `manifest.json`,
  `favicon.png`, `icons/`). It is **not** the React app. The Android/Flutter
  build never touches React source.

## Before changing web code

1. Confirm the file path starts with `D:\Projects\Android-App\ainexus-web\src\`.
2. If you find yourself opening anything under a `web/src` folder, STOP — that is
   the wrong (dead) copy. Port the change to `ainexus-web/` instead.
3. Run the web checks from `ainexus-web/`: `npm run test -- --run` and `npm run build`.
